| Deliberate, not a loophole: since `Log { ... }` is sugar for an object
| literal with "_class" prepended, it is structurally equal to any plain
| object literal that happens to have the same fields in the same order —
| there is no hidden tag distinguishing a "real" particle from a
| hand-written object that looks like one.
assert Log { x = 1 } = { _class = "Log", x = 1 }
assert Log { x = 1 } ≠ Log { x = 2 }
assert Log { x = 1 } ≠ Warn { x = 1 }
